ntrols="primary-navigation" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open menu"><span></span><span></span><span></span></button></div></nav></header><main id="conteudo"><article class="article"><header class="article-header"><div class="wrap article-header-grid"><div><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Blog"><a href="/en/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/en/blog/">Blog</a><span>/</span><span>ERP for small business: what to evaluate before choosing one</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Blog</p><h1>ERP for small business: what to evaluate before choosing one</h1><p class="hero-lead">A practical checklist for evaluating a management system without being distracted by features that do not improve the daily operation.</p><p class="article-byline">Rumman team · Updated 22 July 2026 · 6 min read</p></div><div class="article-symbol" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/blog-spreadsheet.svg" width="240" height="180" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div></header><div class="wrap article-layout"><div class="article-content"><p class="article-intro">The best ERP is not the one with the longest list of features. It is the one that people can use consistently to create reliable history.</p><section><h2>A useful routine</h2><p>Begin with a short, repeatable review. Record the relevant facts close to when they happen, check what is still pending and keep the next action visible to the person responsible.</p></section><section><h2>Decide from current information</h2><p>Reliable records make it easier to compare what was planned with what happened. Review the context before committing to a new sale, purchase, payment or operational promise.</p></section><section><h2>Where Rumman helps</h2><p>Rumman brings customers, operations, inventory, purchases, finance and documents into one guided flow. The final confirmation remains with the person running the business.</p></section><section class="article-sources"><h2>Sources and further reading</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.caixa.gov.br/educacao-fina